<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Paperformat sized for the real SGC document header.

    Why a new record rather than sgc_report_theme_core's "SGC A4 Portrait":
    that one reserves margin_top=28 / header_spacing=24, which is TIGHTER
    than Odoo's stock euro format (40/35). The live 2026-08-01 quotation
    overlapped its title at the stock size already, so adopting the core
    paperformat would have made the collision worse, not better. The core
    record is left untouched - other bridges may legitimately want a compact
    header for short-form documents.

    Sizing rationale: wkhtmltopdf draws the header inside the top margin and
    then leaves the body to start at margin_top; if the rendered header is
    taller than that reservation it is painted over the body, which is
    exactly the "United Arab Emirates" / "Quotation #" overlap. The SGC
    header is logo + company address + customer address + tagline, which
    measures roughly 25mm once sgc_report_documents.scss compacts it. 38mm
    of header space with body starting at 45mm leaves substantial headroom,
    so a company with a longer postal address still cannot collide.

    header_line is off deliberately - sgc_report_documents.scss already draws
    a gold rule under the header, and wkhtmltopdf's own line would double it.
-->
<odoo noupdate="0">

    <record id="paperformat_sgc_documents" model="report.paperformat">
        <field name="name">SGC Documents A4</field>
        <field name="default" eval="False"/>
        <field name="format">A4</field>
        <field name="orientation">Portrait</field>
        <!--
            2026-08-01 correction, measured rather than estimated.

            First pass used margin_top=45 / header_spacing=38 on the theory
            that header_spacing was a gap subtracted from margin_top. It is
            not: Odoo's stock A4 (base.paperformat_euro) runs margin_top=30
            with header_spacing=40 - spacing HIGHER than the margin - and
            that combination is what produced a correctly tight header here.

            margin_top=45 therefore pushed the body 15mm below where stock
            puts it, which at 96 dpi is ~57px of dead white between the
            letterhead rule and the customer address block. Confirmed
            against a live render.

            margin_top is now stock's 30. Side margins stay at 12 (stock's 5
            crowds the page edge) and header_line stays off because
            sgc_report_documents.scss draws the gold hairline itself.
        -->
        <field name="margin_top">30</field>
        <field name="margin_bottom">16</field>
        <field name="margin_left">12</field>
        <field name="margin_right">12</field>
        <field name="header_line" eval="False"/>
        <field name="header_spacing">40</field>
        <!-- Matches the px-based sizing in sgc_report_documents.scss so the
             browser preview and the PDF agree. -->
        <field name="dpi">96</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
